as enterprises move their applications  and services to the cloud  developers need to evaluate and  experiment with new technologies and  tools to figure out what works best for  them  this evaluation process includes tasks  like identifying which cloud providers  to use  trying out new products and learning how  to use new apis  however we know from talking with  developers that this initial evaluation  and setup phase often takes longer than  expected  maybe you run into problems while  getting your development environment set  up like finding the right libraries and  dependencies  you probably don't want to spend hours  trying to install all the right tools or  trying to figure out why the code works  on your friend's machine  but not yours even after setup  switching back and forth between  documentation your ide  your terminal window and your cloud  console can get messy  this is where cloud shell editor comes  into play  cloud shell provides you with command  line access to your cloud resources  directly from your web browser  in cloud shell editor available at  ide.cloud.google.com  extends cloud shell with an online  development environment  powered by the eclipse thea ide platform  cloud shell editor  makes it easy for you to write code  directly from your web browser and  deploy it to the cloud  this online development environment  comes packed with powerful features to  streamline your development workflows  first cloud shell editor integrates  cloud code a set of id plug-ins that  help you stay productive when developing  cloud-native applications  cloud code simplifies kubernetes and  cloud-run development workflows  it allows you to build deploy and debug  your application in just a couple clicks  it also comes packaged with container  tools like mini cubes scaffold  build packs and jib and with its api  explorer  discovering enabling and adding cloud  apis your application is easy  cloud shell editor also has version  control and support for multiple  projects  making it easy for you to collaborate  with teammates  cloud channel editor also has rich  language support for many popular  programming languages  to make it easy for you to write  functional clean and beautiful code  to help you get started we have online  interactive tutorials to get you up to  speed  you can try some of our cloud shell  editor quick starts for google  kubernetes engine  and cloud run with cloud shell editor we  want to make it easy for you to explore  new cloud technologies prototype  applications and do development tasks  directly from your web browser  check it out at ide.cloud.google.com let  us know what you think and stay tuned  for more episodes  [Music]  you
 

